## FAQs

**Do you need to book an escape room date night in advance?**
Not necessarily. Infusion Play at 546 Yates St accepts walk-ins, so you can show up without a reservation. That said, booking ahead at infusion-play.com guarantees your preferred time slot — especially on weekends when demand is higher.

**Is an escape room date night good for a first date?**
It can be excellent. The shared challenge takes pressure off conversation and gives you something to actually do together. It also reveals a lot about how someone thinks and handles a problem, which is useful early on. Just pick an experience that isn't too intimidating for a first meeting.

**What should you wear to an active date night?**
Comfortable clothes you can move in. If you're doing physical challenge rooms like laser mazes or obstacle courses, you want to be able to crouch, step, and move freely. Leave the formal wear at home.

**How long does an active date night at a venue like Infusion Play take?**
It depends on what you book. A single VR session or escape room typically runs 30 to 60 minutes. If you do a bundle like the Challenge plus Immersion package, plan for two or more hours including transitions, snacks, and the inevitable post-game debrief.

**Is VR safe if one of us gets motion sick easily?**
Free-roaming VR — where you're physically walking rather than using a controller to simulate movement — tends to be much easier on people prone to motion sickness than seated VR. It's worth mentioning any concerns to staff before you start so they can point you toward the right experience.

**What makes an active date better than dinner and a movie?**
Passive experiences put you in the same space without requiring you to actually interact. Active experiences — especially ones with shared goals or light competition — create real moments together. The memories are more specific, the conversation afterward is more natural, and the evening tends to feel like an actual event rather than a routine.

**Can active date nights work for couples who've been together a long time?**
Absolutely. Novelty and shared challenge are just as valuable for established couples as for new ones. Doing something neither of you has tried before — or competing against each other in a challenge room — can bring a different energy to a relationship that's settled into routine.

The dinner-and-a-movie formula isn't broken. But if you want a date night that actually creates something — a story, a memory, a moment you'll still reference months later — active experiences are worth choosing instead. Start with an escape room, add some physical challenge, and see what happens.
